Z||000000||Jim's87GT||09-21-2000||08:47 PM||||Can anyone on the forum direct me to a "blow-up" picture of the headlight motor assembly?  I seem to do better with diagrams that text explainations.  The motor on my unit runs after the assembly is in position (up or down).  Some folks say stripped gear and some feel that it's a little retainer on the cam.  How about your opinion (and pictures). Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-21-2000||08:55 PM||||The 87 headlight motor has 3 little plastic slugs inside that fall apart. You can get them and the instructions for installing them for $10 from <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A> ||||reg||1
